Broad idea:
A roguelike dungeon crawler with progression elements, prestigable progress, and deep lore aspects.

Concept
Begin at F0, the surface. Speak with an NPC to being a dungeon. You start off with 0 skill points and all skills are set to level 1 (out of 10).
You enter the dungeon and begin in the center room with various resources and utilities.
An NPC serves as info, a shop, and a quit option. Progress is saved automatically.
A randomly generated layout based on floor size (small, medium, large) is generated with a boss room where the player can descent.
In order to reach the boss the player must complete various puzzles or challenges. The path to the boss room should always be completable(?) should the player properly use their resources.
There should be additional bonus skill-rooms which are unlocked using the various secondary skills the player specs into.
These rooms should provide additional resources, gold, and/or experience to benefit the player as they explore and progress.
Some rooms will not be completable as the dungeon is randomly generated and may expect the player to have certain skills leveled up.
As the player defeats bosses they gain experience points. Points can be spent to increase the level of various skills. Skills should be re-spec-able by spending a point to reset.
Players that spend points to increase certain skills and get lucky or express skill within the game will be able to produce better armor, weapons, or supplies for future runs
As the player descends, the odds of rolling a skill check that is higher than the players skill level increases. Eventually the dungeon will be impossible to complete without escaping and resetting to comeback with higher skills.


Example run:
Player spawns in room, each wall has a door
North door is locked behind Green Key, East door is unlocked, West door is locked behind level 1 mining, South door is unlocked
Player mines the rocks to access west door and gains a little xp, peers into room.
West room has 2 enemies and a chest. Player enters, defeats the enemies, gains a little xp, within the chest is a Green Key
Player returns to the central room and checks the east door. Within the east room is a fishing spot for food and a mining rock for metal
Player collects the fish and mines the ore, then returns to the central room.
Player cooks the fish, success chance based on cooking level. Player smelts ore and turns it into a sword.
Player unlocks North door using Green Key and checks the door. Behind it is a room with only 1 door to the north with an Orange Key locking it.
Player checks South door. The room contains a door to the east and west, the east door is unlocked; the west door requires level 3 mining.
The player checks the east door and sees a room with a puzzle. The player solves the puzzle and receives an Orange Key.
The player returns to the center room, then goes North and unlocks the orange door. Behind this door is the boss room.
The player must defeat the boss to "win". after defeating the boss, they may descend to the next floor or escape. Experience is awarded.